# The windowed app's frame rate in game (run_app.py; Metal; not part of
# --menus, which is headless): Escape through the intro movies, Single Player,
# Play Random Map, Start Game with legion's parity settings (800x600x32), then
# 40 seconds of the game (or of "Choose Civilization", which the render thread
# draws the same way) with nobody at the controls, then quit. run_app.py reads
# the app's own frame stats: the guest's presents a second at 800x600.
# See ../settings.script for the pointer.
timeout 400000
pointer f32 [0x9197a8]+4 [0x9197a8]+8
hold 250
wait frames 30
key ESCAPE
wait 2500
key ESCAPE
wait 2500
key ESCAPE
wait size 1024 768 within 180000
wait 3000
moveby 1 1
wait 300
click 511 268                 # Single Player
wait change within 15000
wait 1000
click 748 145                 # Play Random Map
wait change within 20000
wait 1500
click 644 730                 # Start Game
wait size 800 600 within 60000
wait 40000
dump app-frame-limit
quit
